<!--
  Human_player_husk: a human living in symbiosis with the husk parasite.

  This is a VARIANT of the vanilla Human (VariantOf="Human"). It inherits the human ragdoll, animations,
  health limbs/MedUI, heads, hair, beards, skin colors and voice lines, so clothing and "skin" mods made
  for humans work on it unchanged. The attributes and children below follow docs/NPC_TO_PLAYER.md.

  Deliberate differences from NPC_TO_PLAYER:
  - The <Heads>/<Vars>/<MenuCategory>/<Pronouns>/<HeadAttachments> block (1.5) is copied verbatim from the vanilla
    Content/Characters/Human/Human.xml, NOT from Husk_player.xml: this species uses the human head sheet, hair and
    beards. Re-copy it if a game update changes Human.xml.
  - <ragdolls>/<animations folder="default"> on a variant point to the BASE species (Human) folders,
    not to a Ragdolls folder in this mod (RagdollParams.GetDefaultRagdollParams / AnimationParams.GetAnimParams).
  - CrushDepth is not set to Infinity like Husk_player: the human husk still needs a suit outside the sub.
  - Husk="False" (Husk="True" makes it hostile, like vanilla Humanhusk) but UseHuskAppendage="True": the
    vanilla symbiosis appendage comes from the hh_humanhusksymbiosis affliction (Human_player_husk_symbiosis.xml),
    applied by the regen StatusEffect below. HuskedSpecies points at this species so the appendage is looked up
    in the <huskappendage> element of this file.

  Variant merge rules (Prefabs/IImplementsVariants.cs, CreateVariantXML): attributes override the base,
  child elements are matched by name and position, and an EMPTY child element removes the matching base element.
-->
